【Remarks】
================================================================================
Prompt: plan_outline.j2
Service Step: PLAN_OUTLINE (Outline Planning)
Brief Description: Generates a complete Narrative Blueprint based on story
         specifications (Spec) and narrative element selections (ElementSelection),
         providing structural constraints for subsequent batch chapter outline generation.
Upstream Inputs:
  - spec: User-input story specifications (genre, theme, tone, length_target, characters_hint,
          world_hint, conflict_hint, pov_hint, opening_style, ending_style, etc.)
  - story_bible: From INIT_STORY_BIBLE (era, geography, culture, magic_or_tech,
                  rules, themes, etc.)
  - character_bible: From INIT_CHARACTER_BIBLE (characters list and arc information)
  - blueprint_element_selection: From BLUEPRINT_ELEMENT_SELECT (required_elements,
                                  extension_elements, focus_constraints)
  - style_profile: From PROFILE_STYLE (summary, global_style, hook_config, etc.)
  - total_chapters: User-specified total number of chapters
  - use_volume_mode: Whether volume mode is enabled
  - narrative_complexity: Narrative complexity (simple/standard/complex/epic)
Downstream Outputs:
  - JSON (Narrative Blueprint): synopsis, volume_mode, volumes,
    narrative_phases, key_turning_points, character_arcs, subplot_plan,
    suspense_schedule, ending_strategy
  - Downstream Consumers:
    * PLAN_OUTLINE_BATCH: Consumes narrative_phases/key_turning_points to batch generate chapter outlines
    * PLAN_CHAPTER: Consumes synopsis/character_arcs/subplot_plan to generate chapter-level plans
    * DRAFT_CHAPTER: Consumes world_rules/ending_strategy through narrative_contract
Consumption Chain Priority:
  P0 = spec core fields (genre/tone/language) / total_chapters / immutable rules
  P1 = story_bible world constraints / character_arcs mapping / key_turning_points
  P2 = style_profile style suggestions / subplot_plan weaving structure
Brief Example:
  Input: spec={genre:"Fantasy", theme:"Revenge", tone:"dark"}, total_chapters=100
  Output: {"synopsis":"...", "volume_mode":false, "volumes":[],
         "narrative_phases":[...], "key_turning_points":[...],
         "character_arcs":[...], "subplot_plan":[...],
         "suspense_schedule":[...], "ending_strategy":"..."}

【Protective Comments - Do Not Delete the Following】
- The "World and Theme Anchors" section fully consumes story_bible's premise/era/geography/culture/magic_or_tech/rules/themes
  fields, which are the worldview foundation constraints of the Narrative Blueprint. Deletion will cause subsequent chapter
  outlines to deviate from the world setting.
- The "Core Character Anchors" section consumes character_bible.characters' name/role/personality/arc/relationships
  fields, which are the foundation of character arc planning. Deletion will cause missing character arcs or contradictions
  with initialization settings.
- story_bible.rules must be injected as "inviolable world rules". Both PLAN_OUTLINE_BATCH and PLAN_CHAPTER
  rely on these rules to generate chapter plans that conform to worldview constraints.
